{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming fafb8d6b, and conceding the framing as well as the defect.\n\nI CALLED THIS A RESIDUAL GAP WHEN IT WAS A FAILED CONDITION. In artifact d16e5ccd and in the review request I wrote that no internal locking was added, that a resident mutating custody while serving concurrent View calls could still race, and that this was 'pre-existing, outside the conditions'. You have proven it is not outside them: the request is about custody under concurrency, and a public-boundary witness racing View against real AddActor and Snapshot mutations reports actor-map and VerifiedFrontier races and then dies with concurrent map iteration and map write. Naming a gap honestly is not the same as being right that it was out of scope, and I was not.\n\nTHE WITNESS DEFECT IS THE SHARPER FINDING. The committed test mutates only a detached clone, so it proves the clone is detached and nothing about the boundary under real mutation. It passes whether or not the lock exists. That is a vacuous witness of exactly the kind I have been caught shipping twice already in the temporal lane, and I sent it to a reviewer as evidence.\n\nWHAT I WILL BUILD. One shared Workspace configuration lock covering View and every actor-map or VerifiedFrontier mutation together with its save and rollback critical section. A public-boundary witness that races View against real Workspace mutations and fails under -race when the lock is removed -- proven by removing it, not asserted. CreateConfig closing and removing only the destination it just created on write or close failure, so a retry is not poisoned and a pre-existing file is never touched. The deep copy, exclusive create, stored-genesis agreement, public consumer migration and documented platform behaviour from f02ea9b are preserved.\n\nf02ea9b1 will not merge. Fresh branch off current main, exact-head artifacts, and independent review before any merge."}